\pard\sa200\qc\b\fs44\cf0 AI PROMPT LOG AND GIT COMMIT HISTORY REPORT\par
\pard\ql\b0\fs22\cf1\i Barbon Portfolio \'B4 Laravel + Blade + Tailwind CSS\par
\pard\ql\b0\fs22\cf1\i Gentrix Jay B. Barbon \'B4 BSIT 4 \'B4 IPA Midterm Activity 1\'963\par
\pard\ql\b0\fs20\cf2\i Repository: https://github.com/barbongentrix/barbonportfolio.git\par
\pard\sa300\ql\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa200\b\fs30\PART 1 \'96 AI PROMPT LOG\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22\i Agent used: OpenCode (Big Pickle)\par
\pard\sa300\i0\par

\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 1 \'96 Setting up the Laravel project\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Create a new Laravel project in my folder using the latest stable version, with no database, migrations, or models."\line Result/Output: The agent ran \'93composer create-project laravel/laravel\'94 and created the full Laravel project skeleton (app, bootstrap, config, database, public, resources, routes, storage, tests, vendor).\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 2 \'96 Installing styling dependencies\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Install the Node dependencies so Tailwind CSS can be compiled through Vite."\line Result/Output: The agent ran \'93npm install\'94 successfully (88 packages installed, 0 vulnerabilities).\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 3 \'96 Creating the main Blade layout\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Create a main Blade layout file named layouts/app.blade.php with Tailwind CSS, a sticky navigation bar with links to Home, Education and Projects, a button to my GitHub, and a footer."\line Result/Output: The agent generated the shared layout with a dark theme, responsive navigation, a mobile hamburger menu toggle, and a centered footer.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 4 \'96 Creating routes for the portfolio pages\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Set up routes for the home page, the education page, and the projects page, each returning its own Blade view so every portfolio section is a distinct page."\line Result/Output: The agent updated routes/web.php with three named GET routes: /, /education, and /projects, each passing the current page name so the navigation can highlight the active link.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 5 \'96 Building the Basic Information (Home) page\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Create a responsive Blade home page for my basic information: my name Gentrix Jay B. Barbon, a profile picture, my contact number 09156426499, my location, a short bio saying I am a BSIT student who loves web development, and a section with clickable GitHub repository links shown as styled cards."\line Result/Output: The agent generated the hero section with a gradient ring around the profile image, contact chips with icons, call-to-action buttons, and a GitHub Repositories section with two clickable cards (the barbonportfolio repository and the @barbongentrix profile).\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 6 \'96 Adding the profile picture placeholder\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Add a placeholder profile image in public/images so the site works immediately; I will replace it with my real photo later."\line Result/Output: The agent created an SVG placeholder avatar (gradient background with a silhouette) at public/images/profile.svg.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 7 \'96 Building the Educational Background page\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Create a responsive Blade component for my educational history using Tailwind CSS. It should be a vertical timeline with three entries: College \'97 Data Center College of Bangued (BSIT), Bangued, Abra; Secondary \'97 Little Flower High School; Elementary \'97 Malamsit Elementary School. Include year chips and different accent colors per level."\line Result/Output: The agent generated a vertical gradient timeline with icon markers, a level badge (College / Secondary / Elementary) on each card, degree descriptions, and year chips to be filled in.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 8 \'96 Building the Projects page (empty dashboard)\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Create the projects page as an empty dashboard for now: show a clean empty state message saying there are no projects yet with a link to my GitHub profile, and include a commented-out template card in the Blade file so I can copy it to add project cards later."\line Result/Output: The agent generated a projects grid with a dashed-border empty state (icon, heading, description, and a GitHub button), plus a ready-to-copy commented project card template with title, description, tech tags, and repository link.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 9 \'96 Generating the README.md\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Generate a README.md file describing my portfolio project: project description, features, pages, tech stack, requirements, installation steps, and my author details with my GitHub profile link."\line Result/Output: The agent generated a complete Markdown README with a features table, routes table, tech stack, installation instructions, and a link to PROMPT_LOG.md.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 10 \'96 Version control and Git workflow\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Initialize a git repository, stage everything, and make descriptive commits following my commit message standards like \'91Initial commit: Set up Laravel Blade layout and basic info page\'92. Then connect my public GitHub repository https://github.com/barbongentrix/barbonportfolio.git as origin and push the main branch."\line Result/Output: The agent initialized git, made granular descriptive commits, and connected origin. The final push was completed by the student after signing in with the barbongentrix account.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 11 \'96 Updating the education year labels and chips\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Remove 2021 from college, just put up to present; secondary years attended - 2020; elementary year attended - 2016" followed by "make the years attented to year graduated in secondary and elementary".\line Result/Output: The agent updated the timeline chips: College "Years attended: Up to Present", Secondary "Year graduated: 2020", Elementary "Year graduated: 2016".\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 12 \'96 Adding the Certifications dashboard before Projects\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Put certification dashboard before project."\line Result/Output: The agent created a new /certifications route and dashboard with an empty state and a ready-to-copy card template, placed before Projects in the navigation.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 13 \'96 Adding the Skills dashboard before Certifications\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Put skill dashboard before certifications."\line Result/Output: The agent created a new /skills route and dashboard with an empty state and a skill-category card template with progress bars, placed before Certifications.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 14 \'96 Filling the Skills with the coding skills of the system\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Put contents in skills about coding of this system."\line Result/Output: The agent filled the Skills dashboard with the actual technologies used in building the portfolio, organized into Backend Development (Laravel, PHP/XAMPP/Composer, Routing and Blade), Frontend Development (Tailwind CSS, HTML/CSS, responsive design), and Tools and Version Control (Git and GitHub, npm and Vite, AI-assisted development), each with gradient progress bars.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 15 \'96 Adding the certificate images with their titles\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Put these two certificate images in certifications with their title" (DOST/iHub "Startup Now Cordillera: Exploring Programs, Funding, and Opportunities for Aspiring Startups" and DICT "Understanding Startups and Getting Your Idea Ready for the Philippine Startup Challenge XI" certificates attached).\line Result/Output: The agent cropped the phone screenshots, saved the clean certificate images under public/images/certificates/, and built two certificate cards with thumbnail, title, issuer chip, date chip, and a link to view the full-size certificate.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 16 \'96 Adding the project screenshots with the project title\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Put these two screenshots in projects with the title of QR CODE EVENT ATTENDANCE SYSTEM."\line Result/Output: The agent replaced the empty projects state with a featured full-width project card showing both screenshots (login page and admin dashboard, each clickable to full size), a full description of the system for DCCP-Bangued S.Y. 2025-2026, and technology tags.\par
\pard\sa150\b\fs24 Task 17 \'96 Single-page scrollable redesign\par
\pard\sa100\b0\fs22 Prompt used: "Improve the design and the theme, make it all in one scrollable screen only, but don't remove the navigation dashboard."\line Result/Output: The agent converted all pages into sections of one scrollable home screen using Blade partials (hero, education, skills, certifications, projects, GitHub repositories) with numbered section headers (01-05), improved the theme with gradient hero text, glow background accents, and unified section header dividers, and kept the sticky navigation bar as anchor links with scroll-spy active highlighting and a mobile menu that closes after tapping a link. Old page URLs now redirect to their section anchors.\par
\pard\sa300\par

